      "content_html": "<img src=\"https://cdn.outsideonline.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/all-terrain-chair.jpg\" style=\"width:100%;max-height:300px;object-fit:cover;\"/>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 0.75em;padding:5px 10px;background:#f0f4f8;border-left:3px solid #7b9fc4;border-radius:3px;font-size:0.82em;color:#444;line-height:1.8;\">🪶 🌲 🏔️ 🔭 <a href=\"https://zirnhelt.github.io/super-rss-feed/review.html?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.outsideonline.com%2Fadventure-travel%2Fnews-analysis%2Fnational-park-accessibility-adaptive-wheelchairs%2F\" style=\"color:#7b9fc4;text-decoration:none;\">✏️</a></p>\n<figure><img alt=\"National Parks Are Offering Free Off-Road Wheelchairs. It’s a Game Changer for Families Like Mine.\" src=\"https://cdn.outsideonline.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/all-terrain-chair.jpg?width=1200\"/></figure>\n<p>More than two dozen park sites, including all five of Utah's national parks, now provide adaptive trail equipment. For my son and me, this growing trend meant hiking together without having to turn back.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.outsideonline.com/adventure-travel/news-analysis/national-park-accessibility-adaptive-wheelchairs/\">National Parks Are Offering Free Off-Road Wheelchairs. It’s a Game Changer for Families Like Mine.</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.outsideonline.com\">Outside Online</a>.</p>",
